=== hanbi_hub
@if flag.room_hanbi and not flag.hanbi_postchat
    @show hanbi smile at=c
    > Hanbi is back in his corner of the sofa. The water bottles are gone — handed out, you assume, to people who didn't know they were thirsty.
    > He's drawing. He doesn't look up when you sit down, but he tilts the page towards you, which is the same thing.
    > It's the orange sofa, tiny, in the corner of the page. Two people on it, drawn from behind. The backs of two heads, and a pencil between them.
    you: Is that us?
    > He doesn't answer. He adds a thought bubble over one of the heads. Inside it, very small: a pencil sharpener with a cross through it.
    you: …Okay. That's funny.
    hanbi[smile]: …It never worked.
    @show songha smile at=l
    songha: You two came out of there looking like you'd either been crying or laughing. I can't tell which.
    hanbi: …Neither.
    songha: He says "neither," {{playerName}}, but he's drawing in the lobby.
    songha: When he's in a bad mood, he draws in the stairwell. I've made a note.
    hanbi[shy]: …Songha.
    songha[laugh]: I'm going. I'm going. There's a schedule.
    @hide songha
    hanbi: …He's right. About the stairwell.
    * [sincere] "What did it feel like? Seeing it from the inside?"
        @rel hanbi trust+1
        hanbi[thinking]: …Like finding a page I forgot I'd started.
        hanbi: And someone had already done the hard part.
        you: Which part?
        hanbi[smile]: …Showing up.
    * [playful] "Can I have that one? For my wall."
        @rel hanbi closeness+1
        > He tears the page out along the perforation, slowly, so there isn't a single ragged edge, and hands it to you.
        hanbi: …Don't hang it by a window. It'll fade.
    * [quiet] Lean back and watch him draw.
        @rel hanbi closeness+1
        > He draws. You watch. The lobby noise goes on around you, and none of it gets in.
        > After a while he turns the sketchbook so you can see: he's added a third thing to the sofa. A water bottle. Half full.
    @flag hanbi_postchat
@elif flag.room_hanbi
    @show hanbi smile at=c
    @if rooms() >= 6
        > Hanbi holds up the sketchbook: all eight doors of the hall in a row. The ones that have been opened are coloured in.
        hanbi: …Almost done. Then what?
    @else
        > Hanbi slides a water bottle along the cushion to you without looking up.
        hanbi: …Drink that. You've been talking a lot tonight.
@else
    @show hanbi neutral at=c
    > Hanbi is sharpening a pencil over a folded tissue, so none of the shavings fall on the lobby floor.
    > The building is being gutted in the morning. Nobody would notice. He's careful anyway.
    you: Your door's still there, you know. Whenever you want.
    hanbi: …I know.
    hanbi[thinking]: I'm just getting used to it. The idea of someone seeing it.
    hanbi[smile]: Go see the others. …I'll be here.
    > He holds out a second pencil, freshly sharpened. You don't know what you'll use it for. You take it anyway.
@hub act2

=== hanbi_route
@chapter route
@time 03:50
@var route = "hanbi"
@bg studio_lobby t=fade
@music quiet
@amb night
> Seventy minutes. The others scatter the way people do when they've been told how long they have: slowly, then all at once.
> Hanbi's corner of the sofa is empty. His coat is gone. The water bottles are gone.
> On the armrest, placed very precisely, is a single sharpened pencil. It's pointing at the corridor to the back of the building.
you: …Subtle.
@bg studio_lounge t=fade
@amb room
> The lounge is at the back of the ground floor, behind a door with a round window like a porthole. You haven't been inside the real one since you were sixteen.
> The renovation crew has already been through. Dust sheets over everything — the tables, the armchairs, the shelf of board games nobody ever finished.
> One sheet has been folded back and set on the floor in a neat square.
> Underneath it is the sofa. It is orange. It is, somehow, worse in real life.
@show hanbi smile at=c
> Hanbi sits on it with his sketchbook open, one lamp on, the rest of the room left to the streetlight through the window.
hanbi: …You found it.
you: You left a pencil pointing down the corridor.
hanbi[shy]: …I wanted it to be okay if you didn't come.
you: So you left half an invitation.
